orac-branding (1.2.0-1) umbra; urgency=medium

  * Login message: /etc/motd (console and SSH logins) becomes a link to
    /usr/share/orac/motd, with ORAC as the main feature and Shadowfetch named as
    the base OS. Only the stock Shadowfetch copy (or an empty/missing motd) is
    taken over; it is kept as /etc/motd.pre-orac and put back on remove/purge.
    A hand-edited /etc/motd is left alone.
  * Stop registering the splash as a default.plymouth alternative, and remove
    1.0.0's registration on upgrade: with no other candidate it made ORAC the
    default theme on install. Shadowfetch selects the theme in plymouthd.conf,
    so plymouth-set-default-theme -R orac is still the one way to activate it.
  * Maintainer scripts honour DPKG_ROOT (tests run them against a scratch root).

 -- Rick Masterson <rickm1982@gmail.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 03:50:00 +0000

orac-branding (1.1.0-1) umbra; urgency=medium

  * Terminal branding. /usr/share/orac/fastfetch/{logo.txt,config.jsonc}: ORAC
    block-letter logo in a blue-to-purple gradient with purple keys, replacing
    the Shadowfetch banner once applied. `orac-terminal-theme apply|revert|status`
    switches the invoking user's ~/.config/fastfetch/config.jsonc, keeping the
    first non-ORAC config as config.jsonc.pre-orac. Nothing is written into a
    home directory by the package itself.
  * Konsole: OracVoid colour scheme and an ORAC profile (JetBrains Mono),
    selectable in Konsole; neither is made the default.

 -- Rick Masterson <rickm1982@gmail.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 03:20:00 +0000

orac-branding (1.0.0-1) umbra; urgency=medium

  * First package: Plymouth splash, Plasma look-and-feel with KSplash, and
    three wallpaper sets, built from the ORAC workstation and Plymouth theme
    zips.
  * Plymouth script rewritten against the script plugin's real API: the zip's
    version called Sprite.SetScale and Plymouth.GetTime (neither exists) and
    Plymouth.SetMessageFunction (it is SetDisplayMessageFunction), so its
    progress bar and status line never moved; its password sprites were held in
    function locals and vanished on return.
  * KSplash: font.letterSpacing (a bare letterSpacing stops the QML loading),
    an #AARRGGBB vignette (the zip's #000000AA was fully transparent), and
    dots that follow the session stage.

 -- Rick Masterson <rickm1982@gmail.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:30:00 +0000
